emusic for LazyOS (the `org.lazy.emusic` package)
=================================================

This package combines:

1. emusic (https://github.com/va1erian/emusic), Copyright (c) the emusic
   contributors, under the MIT licence (resources/LICENSE-emusic.txt). Its
   icons (icons/app-*.png) come from the same repository.

2. Symphonia (https://github.com/pdeljanov/Symphonia), the MP3 decoder,
   under the Mozilla Public License 2.0, used unmodified; its source is at
   that address at version 0.6.1.

3. SQLite (public domain), built into emusic's library through rusqlite.

4. The LazyOS platform layer (`emusic/` in the LazyOS tree) and the LazyOS
   libraries it links (`xui-app`, `audioclient`), under the GNU General
   Public License, version 3 or later. The program `bin/emusic.elf` as a
   whole is therefore distributed under the GNU GPL, version 3 or later.

5. The sample track (resources/tones.mp3), generated by
   tools/emusic/make_tones.py: CC0.

Corresponding source
--------------------

The LazyOS tree at the revision this package was built from, plus emusic at
the revision pinned in `emusic/Cargo.toml` (EMUSIC_REV in
tools/emusic/build.py) and the crates in `emusic/Cargo.lock`.
